DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       tteeee()  duplicates up to _s_i_z_e bytes of data from the pipe referred to by
       the file descriptor _f_d___i_n to the pipe referred to by the file  descrip‐
       tor  _f_d___o_u_t.   It  does  not  consume  the data that is duplicated from
       _f_d___i_n; therefore, that data can be copied by a subsequent sspplliiccee(2).

       _f_l_a_g_s is a bit mask that is composed by ORing together zero or more  of
       the following values:

       SSPPLLIICCEE__FF__MMOOVVEE      Currently has no effect for tteeee(); see sspplliiccee(2).

       SSPPLLIICCEE__FF__NNOONNBBLLOOCCKK  Do  not  block on I/O; see sspplliiccee(2) for further de‐
                          tails.

       SSPPLLIICCEE__FF__MMOORREE      Currently has no effect for tteeee(), but may be imple‐
                          mented in the future; see sspplliiccee(2).

       SSPPLLIICCEE__FF__GGIIFFTT      Unused for tteeee(); see vvmmsspplliiccee(2).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       Upon successful completion, tteeee() returns the number of bytes that were
       duplicated between the input and output.  A return  value  of  0  means
       that  there  was  no  data  to transfer, and it would not make sense to
       block, because there are no writers connected to the write end  of  the
       pipe referred to by _f_d___i_n.

       On error, tteeee() returns -1 and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

